From 94bd7a4140bf491a455bbfa0e00829fba431ce02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:36:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the waiting screen (Gibax's mockup); a seat that
 leaves is the AI's

- The relay's WAIT line now carries each seat's state (O expected,
  V there, X left before the start). A seat that leaves no longer holds
  the start: GO comes once no seat is expected, with seat:character/gear
  for each seat that left, a character the relay drew at random (the
  same on every machine; decision of 2026-11-25). The runner sets it
  for the race (srnp::SetSeatChoice) and the relay gives that seat the
  AI flag as its input.
- The waiting screen (srnp_waiting_screen.cpp), from Gibax's mockup:
  "<n> Players", "<n> Racers", "<n>/<n> Ready", then for each seat its
  label (nP, or COM for a seat that left), its character (the name for
  now: the game's heads are not in this repository) and its state (blue
  circle on the way, green tick there, red cross left), "YOU" under this
  machine's seat. While the runner waits for GO in the relay's hook, the
  last frame is presented again with the screen over it, as the menu
  does over a paused game.

Measured: 4 seats, one runner each; seat 1 arrives then is killed:
VOOO, VVOO, VXOO, VXVO, then GO with 1:6/0 (Wave), applied by the three
runners, racer 1 given to the AI; 24 checksums equal, 0 divergences,
0 late inputs. The screen photographed in the real window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
